        "A phone attachment does not turn every ophthalmoscope into a camera",
        "The earlier claim that no suitable phone attachment existed is outdated for PanOptic Plus. The manufacturer’s iExaminer 4.0 instructions document SmartBracket, SmartClip and specified compatible phones. Check the complete supported combination and destination software operation before buying accessories; the documentation is not blanket support for every current phone or older PanOptic. Photographed ophthalmoscopy can support an examination workflow without being equivalent to the retinal imaging service being purchased. Keep the intended examination, documentation and referral use explicit. Across these devices, common batteries and available manuals are practical support clues; no comparative field failure-rate evidence establishes a longest-lasting model."
